            <ArticleTitle>Magnetic resonance imaging of plantar fasciitis and other causes of heel pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>97-107</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Heel pain can be caused by disorders of either the plantar fascia, calcaneus, tendons, or adjacent nerves. Because these conditions can lead to pain located in a small area of the heel, a precise clinical diagnosis may be difficult. This article describes some of these various causes of heel pain and how MR imaging helps to characterize them.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
